# Cloudflare Pages reads a file literally named `_headers` from your build
# output root and applies these rules automatically - no dashboard config
# needed. Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# These two headers make the page cross-origin isolated, which is what
# unlocks SharedArrayBuffer - required for PSP's only available EmulatorJS
# core build (ppsspp-thread-wasm.data). See README "Cross-origin isolation".
#
# IMPORTANT: this project loads EmulatorJS's loader.js and its core/data
# files from cdn.emulatorjs.org (or your own self-hosted /data/ folder).
# COEP: require-corp requires every cross-origin resource on the page to
# either send Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy itself or be fetched with
# crossorigin="anonymous" (which loads CORS-compatible resources fine).
# EmulatorJS's CDN has historically served the necessary CORS headers for
# its own assets, but I have no live network access from this sandboxed
# environment to re-confirm that today - test PSP specifically after you
# deploy, and self-host (see README) if you hit a COEP-blocked resource.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
